From: Ovidijus Vyšniauskas (ovid-io)
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd939x-sdw: program the class-H port's window

The RX data ports are declared SDW_DPN_SIMPLE, and the SoundWire core
only writes DPN_OffsetCtrl2, DPN_BlockCtrl3, DPN_SampleCtrl2 and
DPN_HCtrl for non-simple ports. So the codec's class-H port (DP2) keeps
its reset window, HStart 0 and HStop 15, while the qcom master sends
class-H in the window the DT gives the port (hstart 3, hstop 6 on
SM8650): measured on a KONKR Pocket FIT (WCD9395) with the HiFi PCM
path playing, master HCTRL 0x63, codec DP2 HCtrl 0x0f.

The codec implements those registers. Qualcomm's downstream driver
programs DP2 from its HPH_CLH port table (pineapple-port-config.h: si
63, hstart 3, hstop 6, word length 7, block packing 0), and on stock
Android the same codec reads back HCtrl 0x36 and BlockCtrl3 0 there.

Declare the class-H port SDW_DPN_FULL so both ends agree. The other RX
ports stay simple: the HPH and compander ports have no hstart/hstop in
the DT (0xff), and the HiFi PCM port's window (0/15) already equals the
codec's reset value.

Tested on a KONKR Pocket FIT on Armada 20261109 (this patch built as
the module against its kernel): codec DP2 HCtrl 0x36 and BlockCtrl3 0
while playing, as on Android. Together with the class-H start-up fix
(0083), headphones play clean and loud at full volume.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
index 95f4be2..3e05f6c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x-sdw.c
@@ -61,7 +61,15 @@ static struct sdw_dpn_prop wcd939x_rx_dpn_prop[WCD939X_MAX_RX_SWR_PORTS] = {
 	},
 	{
 		.num = WCD939X_CLSH_PORT,
-		.type = SDW_DPN_SIMPLE,
+		/*
+		 * Not SDW_DPN_SIMPLE: the core only programs OffsetCtrl2,
+		 * BlockCtrl3, SampleCtrl2 and HCtrl for non-simple ports, so the
+		 * codec kept its reset window (hstart 0, hstop 15) while the
+		 * master sends class-H in the hstart/hstop the DT gives it.
+		 * The codec implements these registers: Qualcomm's downstream
+		 * driver programs them (HCtrl 0x36 on SM8650).
+		 */
+		.type = SDW_DPN_FULL,
 		.min_ch = 1,
 		.max_ch = 1,
 		.simple_ch_prep_sm = true,
